      "writtenOn": "2020-03-10T13:58:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The extra dependencies are needed to enforce correct order of graph traversal in GenerateAndroidBuildActions: if X comes before Y on the list of system server jars, build rules (and file paths) for X must be already generated by the time Y is processed (because Y needs those file paths). (Maybe I don\u0027t fully understand you idea about module objects.)\n\nRegarding the dense graph: you are right, there is no need to add transitional dependency edges, e.g for {X,Y,Z} it should be {X\u003c-Y, Y\u003c-Z}, not {X\u003c-Y, Y\u003c-Z, X\u003c-Z}. I should only add one dependency to the previous jar, not to all previous jars. Then the number of edges is linear.",
      "parentUuid": "66599291_166be4bd",
